<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Silures</h1><p class="st-meta">50 BCE – 78 CE (approx.) · capital Llanmelin; later Venta Silurum (Caerwent)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Warlike people of south-east Wales who resisted Rome for nearly thirty years, until legions at Caerleon held their land and Caerwent became their town.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Silures lived in the valleys and coastal plain of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-glamorgan">Glamorgan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gwent">Gwent</a>, defended by hillforts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llanmelin">Llanmelin</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, noting their dark complexions and curly hair, speculated that they had come from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, a guess no longer accepted. They first appear in 47, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> began its advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their leadership; they seem to have been a confederation of communities rather than a single kingdom, without a coinage of their own. Their warfare relied on raids and ambush in difficult country. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caratacus">Caratacus</a> fought alongside them after 47, and in 52 they defeated a legion under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manlius-valens">Manlius Valens</a>; the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-ostorius-scapula">Ostorius Scapula</a> died worn out by the campaign.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sextus-julius-frontinus">Julius Frontinus</a> finally subdued them around 74 to 78 and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> fortress of Isca at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caerleon">Caerleon</a>. Their territory became a civitas within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-britain">Roman Britain</a> with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venta-silurum">Venta Silurum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caerwent">Caerwent</a>, where an inscription records the council of the Silures. The later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-gwent">Kingdom of Gwent</a> grew in the same region.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 50 BCE – 78 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:58.71%;width:2.55%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>50 BCE – 78 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Llanmelin; later Venta Silurum (Caerwent)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>United Kingdom</dd></dl></aside></div>
